  "reasoning": "The product is a fused indole-pyrrolidine system featuring a cyano group on the saturated ring. This architecture is characteristic of a condensation-cyclization reaction between an indole-based primary amine and a nitrile-bearing carbonyl compound. Disconnecting the newly formed C-N and C-C bonds of the five-membered ring reveals tryptamine (providing the indole core and ethylamine side chain) and cyanoacetaldehyde (providing the two-carbon fragment with the nitrile). The forward reaction proceeds via imine formation followed by intramolecular electrophilic aromatic substitution at the indole C3 position to close the ring, releasing water.",
  "final_answer": "N#CC=O.c1ccccc2[nH]c(CCN)cc12"
}

